From 1f819ff065795af920a61fdf493d18347791c7b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dx <dx@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:26:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] macOS window mode: stream and control one window

GET /windows lists on-screen app windows; the dw,<id> command streams one window
(SCContentFilter initWithDesktopIndependentWindow), following its resizes, and
ds,<display> goes back to the display. hello.displays.window names the window;
{"t":"windowClosed","id":N} tells viewers it closed and the stream fell back
to the display. In window mode input maps onto the window's frame, clicks raise
the window and restore the pointer afterwards, and hover and scroll go to the
window's app without moving the pointer.
