diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 067b618..d161b23 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -237,6 +237,19 @@ All viewers follow the selection and reconnect automatically; read-only viewers
 cannot change it. `--display` still selects the initial monitor. The list refreshes
 when capture rebuilds; restart voxl to discover newly attached displays.
 
+Window mode streams and controls one window instead of a whole display (an iOS
+Simulator or Android emulator, say, or any window when you view a Mac from that same
+Mac). `GET /windows` lists the on-screen app windows as `{"windows":[{id, app,
+bundleId, title, frame: {x, y, w, h}, display}]}` (window IDs are CGWindowIDs, frames
+in points). A viewer sends `dw,<id>` to stream a window and `ds,<display id>` to go
+back to a display; every viewer gets a new `hello` whose `displays.window` (`{id, app,
+title}`) names the window, and follows the window's resizes. If the window closes or
+leaves the screen (minimized, another Space), voxl sends `{"t":"windowClosed","id":N}`
+and goes back to the display. Clicks raise the window and put the Mac's pointer back
+where it was when the button is released; hovering and scrolling reach the window's app
+without moving the pointer; keys bring its app to the front. Dynamic resolution is off
+while a window streams.
+
 ```sh
 brew install x264 opus pkgconf esbuild
 cargo build --release
